      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Unlocking _everything_ on the CPU with DRAM scrambling",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/skitter-creek-bath-salts",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/a4zifd",
      "score": 43,
      "comments": 15,
      "author": "radex",
      "published": "2026-08-13T16:06:04Z",
      "bullets": [
        "DRAM bus scrambling can be reverse-engineered, undermining hardware-level memory obfuscation designed to prevent physical bus probing and cold-boot extraction.",
        "Attackers exploiting weak or deterministic PRNGs in memory controllers can reconstruct plaintext data directly from physical DRAM interfaces.",
        "Highlights enclave vulnerabilities (Intel SGX, AMD SEV), proving bus scrambling cannot substitute for authenticated, cryptographically secure memory encryption engines."
      ]
